. 
. /*==============================================================================
>     5. EXTENSION
>     the paper uses only linear probability models with clustered errors.
>     each test below checks one assumption behind those estimates.
>     main specifications: table 3a column (2) for has_debt (sample s_t3_1)
>     and table 4 column (2) for applied_new_bank_loan (sample s_t4_1b).
> ==============================================================================*/
. 
. /*--- E1. Probit and logit vs the linear probability model (ch 17) ---*/
. * H4: the effect of high debt aversion is the same in a probit or logit
. *     model as in the lpm. compare average partial effects (ape).
. 
. foreach y in has_debt applied_new_bank_loan {
  2.     if "`y'"=="has_debt" local s s_t3_1
  3.     else local s s_t4_1b
  4.     if "`y'"=="has_debt" local t hd
  5.     else local t ab
  6. 
.     * lpm, as in the paper
.     eststo e1_lpm_`t': reg `y' i.high_debt_aversion $controls $fe2_dummies if `s', vce(cluster 
> municipality)
  7.     * fitted probabilities outside 0 to 1 (a known weakness of the lpm)
.     predict phat_`t' if e(sample), xb
  8.     count if phat_`t' < 0 & e(sample)
  9.     scalar n_below_`t' = r(N)
 10.     count if phat_`t' > 1 & phat_`t' < . & e(sample)
 11.     scalar n_above_`t' = r(N)
 12.     display "`y': fitted values below 0 = " n_below_`t' ", above 1 = " n_above_`t'
 13. 
.     * probit and logit; margins gives the average partial effect of the dummy
.     probit `y' i.high_debt_aversion $controls $fe2_dummies if `s', vce(cluster municipality)
 14.     eststo e1_probit_`t': margins, dydx(high_debt_aversion) post
 15.     logit `y' i.high_debt_aversion $controls $fe2_dummies if `s', vce(cluster municipality)
 16.     eststo e1_logit_`t': margins, dydx(high_debt_aversion) post
 17. }

